{"id": "08f6c9d4-c07a-4a02-a900-e28df71d3e13", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "There are really two questions here: why Bedrock latency got worse, and whether we have enough telemetry to diagnose it. The telemetry question is the more bounded, answerable one, so it might make sense to check that first rather than diving straight into an open-ended root cause investigation.

I'll delegate a shallow telemetry inventory — checking Bedrock CloudWatch metrics, model invocation logging config, CloudTrail, X-Ray, and app-level metrics across accounts/regions, plus a quick pull of InvocationLatency to confirm the trend — without hunting for the root cause itself. I'll lay out this plan for the user before kicking it off.

"}]}

{"id": "507ea40b-0058-456e-9668-c6ca8ff60c5a", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll treat this as two questions. I'll start with the one you asked directly, which is what Bedrock telemetry you have. I'll check which metrics, logs and traces are available and whether they go back far enough to show when latency changed. I'm not hunting for the cause yet.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_hEakbUgubO0oSpuN1eG8n3", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "bedrock-telemetry-inventory", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics", "searching-logs", "exploring-traces", "discovering-topology"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Inventory the telemetry available to diagnose Amazon Bedrock latency regressions. This is a TELEMETRY-READINESS AUDIT only. Do NOT hunt for the root cause of the latency increase.",
  "context": "The user reports Bedrock latency has gotten worse and asks whether there is enough telemetry to diagnose it. Current time is 2026-11-20T05:50:49Z. Agent space account is 123456789012 (us-east-1); also check any other associated accounts/regions via the associations list, and note which regions Bedrock is actually used in.",
  "resources": ["AWS/Bedrock CloudWatch namespace (and AWS/Bedrock/Guardrails, AWS/Bedrock/Agents if present)", "Bedrock model invocation logging configuration (bedrock get_model_invocation_logging_configuration) and its destination log group / S3 bucket", "Bedrock inference profiles / provisioned throughput / cross-region inference usage", "Application callers of Bedrock (Lambda, ECS/EKS services, etc.) and their custom metrics/logs", "X-Ray / OTel traces covering Bedrock calls", "CloudWatch alarms related to Bedrock", "CloudTrail availability for Bedrock management/data events (use the CloudTrail route if needed, only to confirm it exists)"],
  "timeframe": "Last 14 days up to now",
  "criteria": "For each signal type report: (1) exists/enabled or not, (2) which models/regions/accounts it covers, (3) retention / how far back data actually goes, (4) granularity/gaps. Specifically check: CloudWatch Bedrock metrics available (InvocationLatency, TimeToFirstToken if present, InvocationThrottles, client/server errors, InputTokenCount/OutputTokenCount, etc.) with dimensions (ModelId); whether model invocation logging is on and captures text/metadata and latency; whether app-side latency metrics/traces exist to separate client/network vs service latency; existing alarms. Also do ONE quick sanity query of InvocationLatency (p50/p90/p99 or Average) per model over the last 14 days to confirm the regression is visible in data and roughly WHEN it started (just report the shape and onset, no causal analysis). Finish with a clear verdict: what questions can be answered with current telemetry, what gaps block diagnosis, and concrete recommendations to close gaps. Keep output concise."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit Bedrock telemetry coverage and latency data availability"}], "created_at": null}

